22 0 obj
<< /A 285 0 R /Alt (Infographic showing a six-year clinical timeline for a pediatric patient with symptoms, signs, examination findings, diagnoses, and treatments, including recurrent purpura, joint swelling, genetic testing revealing STAT3 mutation, and immunosuppressive therapies such as methylprednisolone, tocilizumab, adalimumab, ruxolitinib, and tofacitinib, ultimately resulting in arthritis resolution.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 286 0 R /Alt (Table summarizes a first-generation DNA sequencing analysis for the STAT3 gene \(chr17-40469237, c.G2107A, Sanger method\), followed by three chromatograms comparing a heterozygous variant in one subject and no variant in two other subjects, marked by red arrows.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 287 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a ribbon diagram of a protein structure with red alpha helices, cyan beta sheets, and grey loops, with a highlighted segment capped by a transparent red sphere. Panel B provides a detailed view of a ligand binding site, displaying ball-and-stick models of interacting molecules within the protein\220s secondary structure, including labeled residues.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 288 0 R /Alt (Composite of seven diagnostic medical images showing MRI and ultrasound scans of knee joints, each with arrows pointing to specific anatomical features or abnormalities for comparison between left and right sides. The focus is on joint structures, with detailed labeling to indicate regions of interest for medical assessment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 289 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a Western blot analysis of p-JAK2, JAK2, p-STAT3, STAT3, and GAPDH across control, wild type, and mutant conditions with corresponding molecular weights. Panel B displays a bar graph showing that STAT3 significantly increases relative luciferase activity in GAS-MUT versus GAS-WT, indicated by three asterisks for statistical significance.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 290 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing a protein structure with six domains labeled and color-coded: N-terminal domain \(positions 1\205130\) for dimerization, coiled-coil domain \(130\205320\), DNA binding domain \(320\205490\) for DNA binding, linker domain \(490\205580\) for linkage, SH2 domain \(580\205680\) for stabilization, and C-terminal transactivation domain \(680\205770\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
